(AI-Assisted Personalized Learning and Student GPA Performance in Higher Education) Tj T*
(Authors: Pham, D. A., Hoang, B. N., & Vu, T. L. \(2024\)) Tj T*
(Journal: Education and Information Technologies, 29\(4\), 4815-4836.) Tj T*
(DOI: https://doi.org/10.1007/s10639-024-12580-3) Tj T*
(---------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(ABSTRACT:) Tj T*
(This longitudinal study evaluates how structured AI tutoring and self-regulated) Tj T*
(AI usage frequency affect semester Grade Point Average \(GPA\) across disciplines.) Tj T*
(Sample size: N = 510 students across Computer Science, Economics, and Social Sciences.) Tj T*
(---------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(KEY EMPIRICAL FINDINGS:) Tj T*
(1. GPA Improvement: Moderate, structured AI usage \(4 to 8 hours/week\) was associated) Tj T*
(   with an average GPA increase of +0.34 points \(on a 4.0 scale\) compared to non-users.) Tj T*
(2. Optimal Usage Pattern: Students using AI 'Frequently' \(3-5 days/week\) achieved the) Tj T*
(   highest mean GPA \(3.42\), outperforming both 'Rarely' \(2.88\) and excessive passive users.) Tj T*
(3. Positive Correlation: Overall guided AI study hours showed a moderate positive) Tj T*
(   correlation with academic GPA \(r = 0.58, p < 0.001\).) Tj T*
